WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.970
If conservative news were your

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:03.860
only source for information

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.220
You might be thinking that conservatives, and America as a whole

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:12.240
Are under siege by gangs of deranged, violent, blood-thirsty left-wingers

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.000
Teeming with hatred

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.580
Hell-bent on destruction

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.540
And being cheered on by the Democratic Party and the Liberal media

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.360
The Kathy Griffin beheading incident

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:21.860
 

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.640
Antifa protests

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.440
The rendition of Cesar with a Trump character

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.840
And much more seriously, the recent shooting of Republican Congressman Steve Scalise

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.980
At a Republican baseball team practice

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.555
Are all being held up as

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.840
evidence by right-wing pundits

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.320
of violence, hatred, and extremism

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.000
being rampant on the left.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.740
And that Liberal Ideology poses a grave danger  to the country

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.640
Let' s be clear; the threat of violence from people on the left

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.640
should be of concern and monitored closely

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.440
Particularly after the shooting of Steve Scalise

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.520
but there has been a torrent of hysterical coverage

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.360
Night after night

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.060
From Fox News and other right-wing outlets

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.800
that is vastly overblown, sensationalized

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.320
Toxic and horribly hypocritical

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.160
and it ignores the disproportionately high amount of  of right-wing violence

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.000
that we have seen for many years

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.400
and unfortunately it's been pervading the narrative

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.420
among the right.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:26.400
To give you a sense of just how out of hand this narrative has gotten in right-wing media,

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:27.700
Listen to this,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.580
Foul language, directed right at our president,

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.080
They hate him!

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.160
And now, top Republican Steve Scalise is in the hospital.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.000
his condition downgraded to critical.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.060
A Trump hater, a leftist, did this.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.800
Were it not for the bravery of police officers,

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.740
it would have been a massacre of Republicans.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.060
There is a link between the climate of violence,

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.600
and the violent attack on Republicans.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.740
It is a link the left should acknowledge, but they will not.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.080
Instead, Democrats are pushing impeachment.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.340
and the media has returned to pejorative leaks,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.840
which imply the president obstructed justice.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.660
Barely hours after a political shooting,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:12.180
the left wing and the media get right back on track with partisan attacks

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:17.020
and not a word of remorse for the climate of violence they did so much to create

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.440
Look, the tumultuous, polarized political climate we live in today,

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:23.780
is a problem.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.260
Violent rhetoric and political hatred on both sides are disturbing.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.760
and we should have conversations about how to simmer it down.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.420
But this sort of ludicrous, hypocritical coverage from Fox and other right wing media,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.540
only serves to exacerbate the root cause of this violence and hatred.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:46.260
the problem they claim to be trying to solve.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:52.280
For conservative pundits to sit around and cherry pick violent rhetoric or actions

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.260
from a few people who are, broadly speaking, ostensibly on the left,

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.900
while pretending that violent rhetoric is somehow unique to the left,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.180
and a new phenomenon that the right is immune to,

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.260
is disingenuous at best and malicious at worst.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.500
The dillusion and hypocrisy involved in this narrative,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.700
are so striking that it's difficult to even know where to begin.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:21.160
But let's start with the idea that the biggest threat of politcal violence today comes from the left.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.600
and look at that claim empirically.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.640
NPR recently talked to experts who study violence and extremism,

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.760
in order to fact check the claim that left wing political violence is on the rise.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.220
NPR determined that, quote,

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:41.960
those who track extremism say that while there are a few far-left groups that raise red flags

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.260
their numbers remain small

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.220
The groups being referred to  largely fall under the umbrella of Antifa

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.040
short for Anti-fascist.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.340
The NPR article describes antifa as, quote,

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.360
loosely affiliated groups of mostly young people

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.300
mainly on the west coast, but spreading around the country,

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:04.060
They dress in black and wear masks when they confront right-wing groups

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.700
In the past few months there have been clashes and confrontations in Berkeley, California,

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:14.820
Portland, Oregon, and more recently on the campus of Evergreen State College. in Olympia, Washington.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.920
However these incidents have caused conservative pundits like Tucker Carlson,

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:25.520
to lose their minds, and use the ammunition to fan the flames of the quote,

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.160
violent left narrative.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.780
Some of these antifa clashes since Trump was elected,

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.000
have resulted in broken property,

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.060
rocks being thrown, some minor injuries,

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:41.020
No one has been killed or seriously injured during any of these clashes, but nonetheless,

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:45.780
these sort of groups and their tactics should be condemned and monitored appropriately.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:52.420
But Mark Pitcavage, a senior research fellow at the Anti Defamation League's Center on Extremism,

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:56.900
told NPR that the number of far-left, antifa type extremists,

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.920
is tiny in relation to the mainstream political left.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.080
Quote, "the far left is very active in the United States."

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.540
"but it hasn't been particularly violent for some time."

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:13.240
"In the past 10 years when you look at murders committed by domestic extremists,"

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.820
"in the United States, of all types,"

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.040
"right-wing extremists are responsible for about 74% of those murders."

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.240
said Pitcavage to NPR.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.480
This is the crazy part.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:31.700
Despite the alarmism, and hysteria, and sensationalized fear-mongering,

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.840
about left wing violence

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.760
The empirical truth of the matter is that far right extremism,

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:42.180
has been and continues to be a far more significant threat

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:48.220
than far left extremism, even during the age of Trump and the "resistance"

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.160
Ryan Mauro, who I've interviewed before,

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:53.540
is a security analyst with the Clarion Project,

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.600
a right-wing think tank dedicated to, quote,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.600
"Challenging Radical Islam"

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.240
appeared on Fox news recently and said, quote,

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:04.760
"Anyone that studies this kind of extremism or terrorism,"

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:10.580
"knows that whatever political party or philosophy does not control the White House, "

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.060
"The extremism rises on that side."

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.440
But even if we take Mauro at his word here,

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:21.840
right-wing extremism still remains a significantly greater threat

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:25.120
according to experts and all available statistics.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:30.200
What exactly qualifies as right-wing or left-wing extremism?

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.840
What violent incidents are counted in the sum total?

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.200
How the severity of the threat is gauged?

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:40.900
These sorts of variables vary between organizations that study extremism.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.340
But by any metric,

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:47.240
Right wing extremism is definitively, and undeniably a far greater threat.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:51.200
So much so, that it's more or less on par with

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.200
the threat posed by jihadist, Islamic extremism in this country.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.720
And you might be thinking, David, no way, that's an exaggeration,

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:00.480
fake news maybe.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:06.760
Since 9/11 there have been more deadly attacks committed by far right extremists in the US

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.900
than by radical Islamists.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.520
Although more people in total have been killed by Muslim terrorists.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:16.340
According to figures from an exhaustive study by New America,

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.680
which have been updated into 2017

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:25.220
There have been at least 20 deadly attacks motivated by far right wing ideologies in the US since 9/11.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.920
Resulting in the deaths of 53 people.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:32.680
Comparatively, there have been 11 deadly attacks motivated by radical Islam,

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.940
resulting in 95 deaths.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:40.700
To give you a sense of what sorts of incidents New America is categorizing as far right-wing attacks,

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:46.340
Some examples are the stabbing of two men in Oregon this year by Jeremy Joseph Christian,

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.920
an anti-Muslim, anti-Semitic, Nazi sympathizing bigot,

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.980
who was harassing a Muslim girl prior to the stabbing.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:58.520
In March 2017, Timothy Caughman, a black man from New York City,

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:04.260
was stabbed to death with a sword, by James Harris Jackson, a white man from Baltimore, Maryland.

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:06.640
Who drove all the way to New York City,

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.880
with the sole purpose of killing a random and innocent African American.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:17.740
In 2015, three people were killed in a Colorado Springs, Planned Parenthood Clinic

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.300
in a religiously motivated shooting.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:24.500
And of course, 9 black Americans were killed in a Church

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.720
in Charleston, South Carolina by Dylan Rouf,  a white supremacist.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:33.460
The list goes on and on, and these are just the deadly attacks that we're talking about.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:36.720
It doesn't include assaults that result in death,

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:41.300
nor the dozens of right-wing plots that were foiled by law-enforcement.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:45.220
Such as Robert Doggart, a former congressional candidate from Tennessee

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:48.420
who plotted to carry out an armed attack

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:52.760
against a Muslim majority town in rural upstate New York.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:58.180
A study from the Investigative Fund and the National Institute that came out this year,

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.320
found that between 2008 and 2016,

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:07.180
far right plots and attacks outnumbered Islamic instances by almost 2 to 1.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:13.480
The Southern Poverty Law Center has compiled a comprehensive list of right-wing terrorism plots and attacks

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.600
dating back to 1995.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:20.160
and the sheer volume and regularity of these instances is striking.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:24.280
This is a well established issue in the United States.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:28.180
There's numerous available studies and reports going back over the years

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:30.880
that have all come to similar conclusions.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:38.880
These studies include, a 2015 study from the Triangle Center on Terrorism and Homeland Security and Duke University,

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.220
titled, Law Enforcement Assessment of the Violent Extremism Threat,

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:46.880
a 2009 Department of Homeland Security study, titled,

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:54.820
Rightwing Extremism: Current Economic and Political Climate Fueling Resurgence in Radicalization and Recruitment

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:58.260
a 2012 congressional research service report, titled,

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.600
The Domestic Terrorist Threat: Background and Issues for Congress

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.400
a 2011 study done in conjunction between the Department of Homeland Security and

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:12.680
the national consortium for the study of terrorism and responses to terrorism,

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:17.940
and a 2002 FBI report to the senate intelligence committee.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:23.660
Right wing, extremist violence is not just a problem in the United States,

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:28.300
just recently a far right extremist was arrested in France

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:33.940
for plotting to assassinate newly elected French president Macron in front of Donald Trump.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:42.740
and said, after he was arrested, that he wanted to attack, quote, "Muslims, Jews, blacks, and homosexuals."

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:49.420
A right wing terrorist in the UK plowed a van into a crowd of people leaving a mosque in June

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:54.340
A rightwing extremist threw acid into the face of two Muslims in London

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.580
seriously maiming and disfiguring them

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:02.980
So yes, anti-Muslim, anti-black, anti-Semitic, anti-government,

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.140
anti-abortion,

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:07.780
ultra Christian type extremists

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.860
represent a similar threat to jihadist terrorism

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.440
and that threat is not going away any time soon.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:19.300
Experts actually worry that Donald Trump's victory has emboldened these kinds of groups,

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:23.440
and we've seen early evidence of upticks in those types of hate crimes and attacks.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.840
but Fox News and other right wing media outlets ignore this threat.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.580
instead, focusing on the so-called violent left.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:36.540
In fact, the notion that far right extremist represents a major threat,

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.000
is scoffed at on their network.

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:41.080
It's not just Fox News,

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:47.760
Far right wing extremism has been shamefully, a severely under reported issue in the mainstream media in general

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:52.940
Particularly when compared to the sensationalized, fear mongering coverage

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:54.740
of Islamic terrorism

00:11:54.740 --> 00:12:01.040
Another terrifying facet of this, is that the Trump administration has recently frozen funding

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:04.900
slated by President Obama to go to organizations

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.760
that work to counter right wing extremism

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:12.760
but now, let's look at the claim being made by many on the right,

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:18.400
that the Liberal Media is complicit in this supposed rise of hatred and violence on the left

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.880
where we truly get to the height of hypocrisy,

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:23.800
Sean Hannity has said,

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:26.540
that liberals, particularly in the media,

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:31.100
have been dehumanizing and objectifying Republicans.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:34.280
He also wrote in a column for Fox News, titled,

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:38.380
Left wing Haters Fan the Flames of Rage and Violence,

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:42.400
that they, referring I guess, to the left in general,

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:48.440
may not be responsible for violence, but they have a responsibility to dial down the hate

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.280
before more people get hurt.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:55.620
Do you believe there's a link between the climate of hate for Muslims at Fox

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:59.660
and other conservative media, quote, did so much to create?

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:03.320
And the many attacks and plots against Muslim Americans,

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.540
perpetrated by far right radicals?

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:10.680
and Sean, you want to talk about dehumanizing and  objectifying people?

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.060
Look at how you've personally covered Muslims on your show

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.920
(Hannity): Here's what's eventually gonna happen

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.300
Eventually the world's gonna wake up to what I would say.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:22.920
and every radical Islamist like you will be wiped off the face of the earth

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:26.080
(David): and look at how you talk about refugees.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:31.200
(Hannity): ISIS and Al Qaeda, not if, they will infiltrate the refugee community,

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:35.080
this president is committed to nearly 250,000 coming to America.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:40.840
(David): and just look at the kind of hateful, sometimes violent rhetoric, espoused by people

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:44.420
on your side during the 8 years that Obama was president.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:48.600
"He's a secret Muslim that wants to enact Sharia Law,"

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:51.360
"He's a traitor, he hates America."

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:55.020
And this wasn't only a problem when Barack Obama was president

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:56.880
It's still a problem right now.

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:00.700
Within days of the shooting at the Republican baseball practice,

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:03.540
Former Republican congressman Joe Walsh tweeted,

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:06.260
"Screw talks of bipartisanship"

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:12.000
"This country is at war with itself.  Choose your side and choose it now"

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.280
"Grab your musket and get ready."

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:20.380
It's always wise not to throw stones when you live in a glass house.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.820
and the audacity of these conservative pundits,

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:27.480
to lecture the left about toning down the rhetoric,

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.080
is incredible.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.640
and it's just conservative pundits in the media.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:35.160
I mean, Donald Trump himself has openly and brazenly

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:38.800
encouraged violence against demonstrators at his rallies.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:43.900
(Trump): I love the old days. You know what they used to do to guys like that in a place like this?

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.160
They'd be carried out in a stretcher folks.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.520
(applause)

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:52.200
(David): This rhetoric did materialize into real violence

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:55.880
A number of demonstrators exercising their right to free speech

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.780
that conservatives love to champion,

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:01.380
were assaulted and injured at Trump rallies

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.500
after Donald Trump literally called for it.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:10.620
Trump campaign rallies often devolved into cesspools of depraved hatred.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:15.080
Where legitimately vile, scornful, violent rhetoric

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.600
was openly espoused by Trump supporters.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:20.020
Politico reported that during the campaign

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:23.180
that refrains of 'hang the bitch' and 'kill the bitch'

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:27.360
were growing increasingly common at Trump rallies, referring of course, to Hillary Clinton.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:31.080
A Trump supporter was photographed wearing a shirt that said,

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:35.640
Rope. Tree. Journalist. Some assembly required.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:41.080
Curt Schilling, a former major league baseball pitcher, turned conservative mouthpiece,

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.700
shared it on twitter, and thought it was funny.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:48.620
Where were all of these conservative pundits talking about toning down the rhetoric then?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:53.060
This widespread, hateful, anti-media rhetoric

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:55.940
has also materialized into real violence.

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.780
Then republican candidate Greg Gianforte,

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.080
body slammed a reporter

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:03.620
and then won a congressional race the next day.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:07.620
We're not talking about dolls and plays here.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:11.420
We're talking about instances of real, physical violence.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:17.520
corresponding to legitimately hateful rhetoric that's widespread in conservative discourse.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.780
And remember when Trump said,

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:22.620
that the second amendment people might need to

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.100
stop Hillary Clinton from appointing liberal justices to the Supreme Court?

